[require map::box::store::fs [opt [vset VERSION]]]
[description]

This package provides a store of [term geo/box] definitions, loaded from the [term geo/box] files
(see [package map::box::file]) found in a directory of the filesystem.

[para] The store is a basic example of a [term geo/box] store, and defines the [sectref {Store API}]
expected from the backing store of a [package map::box::store::memory].

[section API]

[list_begin definitions]

[call [cmd ::map::box::store::fs] [arg storeName] [arg directory] [opt [arg options]...]]

Creates a new store object named [arg storeName], and returns the fully qualified name of its
command. The [arg storeName] can be [const %AUTO%] to generate a unique name.

[para] All files in [arg directory] matching the [option -pattern] are read with
[cmd {map box file read}]. Files which cannot be read, or are not valid [term geo/box] files, are
ignored. Subdirectories are not searched. The files are read only once, at creation, later changes
to the directory are not seen by the store.

[para] The only option is

[list_begin options]
[opt_def -pattern [arg pattern]]
The glob pattern selecting the files to read in [arg directory]. Defaults to [const *.box]. This
option is read-only, it can only be set at creation.
[list_end]

[call [arg storeName] [method ids]]

Returns a list of the ids of all [term geo/box]es in the store, in dictionary order. The id of a
[term geo/box] is the path of the file it was read from, i.e. [arg directory] joined with the name of
the file.

[call [arg storeName] [method get] [arg id]]

Returns the [term geo/box] with the given [arg id], a dictionary with keys [const names] and
[const geo], as described in [package map::box::file]. Throws an error if the [arg id] is not known.

[call [arg storeName] [method visible] [arg geobox]]

Returns a list of the ids of all [term geo/box]es which have at least one of their four corners
inside the geographical box [arg geobox] (a list of minimal latitude, minimal longitude, maximal
latitude and maximal longitude). Note that a [term geo/box] overlapping [arg geobox] is not
reported if none of its corners is inside, e.g. when it contains [arg geobox] completely.

[call [arg storeName] [method cget] [arg option]]

Returns the value of the [arg option].

[call [arg storeName] [method destroy]]

Destroys the store.

[list_end]

[section {Store API}]

The methods [method ids], [method get], and [method visible] described above are the API of a
[term geo/box] store, used by [package map::box::store::memory] to access its backing store. Any object providing these methods can be used in place of
[package map::box::store::fs], for example a store backed by a database. Such a store must
satisfy:

[list_begin definitions]
[def "[arg store] [method ids]"]
Returns a list of the ids of all [term geo/box]es in the store. The ids are arbitrary strings,
unique within the store.

[def "[arg store] [method get] [arg id]"]
Returns the [term geo/box] with the given [arg id], a dictionary containing at least the keys
[const names] (a list of names) and [const geo] (a list of minimal latitude, minimal longitude,
maximal latitude and maximal longitude), see [package map::box::file]. Further keys are allowed, and
are passed through by [package map::box::store::memory].

[def "[arg store] [method visible] [arg geobox]"]
Returns a list of the ids of the [term geo/box]es to show in a map whose visible part is the
geographical box [arg geobox].
[list_end]

[para] The store must be given to the users as the name of a single command, a command prefix with
arguments is not supported.

[section EXAMPLE]

[example_begin]
package require map::box::store::fs

map box store fs Boxes /path/to/directory

foreach id [lb]Boxes ids[rb] {
    set box [lb]Boxes get $id[rb]
    puts "$id: [lb]join [lb]dict get $box names[rb] {, }[rb] [lb]dict get $box geo[rb]"
}

# The boxes with a corner in the area of Vancouver
puts [lb]Boxes visible {49.19 -123.27 49.32 -123.02}[rb]
[example_end]

